sequenceDiagram
    actor Requester
    participant Orders as Order service
    participant Supplier as Supplier Service
    participant Users as User Service
    participant Rating as Rating Service
    participant Credit as Credit Service
    participant DB as Postgres

    Requester->>Orders: POST /api/v1/orders
    Orders->>Orders: check expiry and delivery times
    Orders->>Users: GET /internal/users/{userId}/telegram
    Users-->>Orders: telegram handle
    Orders->>Supplier: GET /api/v1/supplier/{pickupId}
    Supplier-->>Orders: approved place
    Orders->>DB: validate delivery point id or inline geofence
    Orders->>Rating: GET /api/v1/rating/{userId}
    Rating-->>Orders: average (or null)
    Orders->>Credit: POST /api/v1/credit/internal/reserve
    Credit-->>Orders: reserved
    Orders->>DB: insert/fork dropoff if needed, CREATED order, usage upsert, log, alert, status outbox
    Orders-->>Requester: 201 CREATED
    Note over Orders,Credit: If the insert fails, POST /api/v1/credit/internal/release returns the reservation
